/T (Agent Pools in Azure DevOps are collections of agents that execute the tasks defined in your CI/CD pipelines. An agent is an application installed on a physical or virtual machine that runs builds, deployments, or other automated tasks defined in your pipelines. Agent pools allow you to manage and organize these agents into groups, facilitating the allocation of the necessary resources for pipeline execution.)
/E (Agent Pools in Azure DevOps are collections of agents that execute the tasks defined in your CI/CD pipelines. An agent is an application installed on a physical or virtual machine that runs builds, deployments, or other automated tasks defined in your pipelines. Agent pools allow you to manage and organize these agents into groups, facilitating the allocation of the necessary resources for pipeline execution.)
